    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493313670/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Thursday, Dec. 26, 1907
Heavy and rainy.
Karin, Algar.
Went to Academy with Algar and Miss Brown. The doctor came when we got back and saw Karin’s boil, and found it was an abscess.
B.B. also has a boil, and neither of the poor things can sit normally on their chairs.
Bernhard remarked, “Our fathers have eaten sour grapes and their children are set on edge.”
Algar and Karin and I played Cutthroat Bridge in evening and discussed Free Will."""^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 382 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1907> .

